  "result": "The gate never judged the concept: both runs returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION`, and the file it flagged wasn't one I wrote. Each time the shell tool runs a command, including the gate itself, it saves the output to a file under `.runtime/tmp/…/tasks/<id>.output` inside the repo. The gate counts that file as a change outside the concept's files. My only allowed command is the gate, so I can't delete these files, and every further run makes a new one. I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs.\n\n**Concept body:** with h as a's heading and d as r's lane direction, both read normalised, the body is three conditions joined by \"and\":\n- d · h > 0\n- d_x·h_y − d_y·h_x < −sin_tol\n- `kin_speed a` > speed_tol\n\nIt uses only the three claimed atoms, the formals and the two parameters. The only number in it is zero. The contract left no choices open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses:**\n- **Setup:** an east-pointing lane 100 (x 0–100 m, y 0–4 m), with motor vehicle 1 inside it at 10 m/s. The instance sets sin_tol = 1/10 and speed_tol = 1 m/s.\n- **holds:** heading (4/5, −3/5), so the cross product is −3/5, below −1/10. Expected: holds.\n- **fails:** heading east, so the cross product is 0. Expected: fails.\n- **blind:** the holds scene with `st.lane_direction` masked. Expected: unknown.\n\nThese are untested, since the gate stopped at the scope check.\n\n**Needed in the harness:** the scope check should ignore the shell tool's `.runtime/tmp` directory, or that directory should move outside the repo. Otherwise the harness's own gate run after this session will fail the same way.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- `task_result.md`\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/lane/heading_right_of_carrier.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/lane/heading_right_of_carrier.lean`",
